      "hints": [
        "Complete the square: $g(x) = (x - 3)^2 - 2$.",
        "Isolate $x = 3 + \\sqrt{y + 2}$ to get $g^{-1}(x) = 3 + \\sqrt{x + 2}$.",
        "State domain of $g^{-1}$ as $x > -1$ (from $g(4) = -1$)."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Complete the square for $g(x) = x^2 - 6x + 7$:\n$$g(x) = (x - 3)^2 - 9 + 7 = (x - 3)^2 - 2$$",
        "Set $y = (x - 3)^2 - 2$ and solve for $x$ on the domain $x > 4$ (where $x - 3 > 1 > 0$):\n$$(x - 3)^2 = y + 2 \\implies x - 3 = \\sqrt{y + 2} \\implies x = 3 + \\sqrt{y + 2}$$\n$$g^{-1}(x) = 3 + \\sqrt{x + 2}$$",
        "Determine the domain of $g^{-1}$ from the range of $g$ on $x > 4$:\n$$x > 4 \\implies x - 3 > 1 \\implies (x - 3)^2 > 1 \\implies (x - 3)^2 - 2 > -1$$\n$$\\text{Domain of } g^{-1}: \\quad x > -1 \\quad (\\text{or } (-1, \\infty))$$"
